        "original_id": "fc167cd7-6c25-53f6-b6b0-2f8612394bee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Vienna Sezession\n- Events: 14th Exhibition of the Vienna Sezession\n- Places: Vienna, Western society\n- Concepts: Wiener Werkstätte Style, Modernism\n- People: Viennese artists\n\nFacts:\n- In 1902, the 14th Exhibition of the Vienna Sezession marked the beginning of the emergence of the radical distinctiveness of certain Viennese artists.\n- The radical distinctiveness of certain Viennese artists helped set a foundation for the widespread Modernist movement.\n- Modernism is a philosophical movement.\n- Modernism arose alongside cultural trends and changes from wide-scale, far-reaching transformations in Western society during the late 19th and early 20th centuries.",
